  "summary": "A ceremonial woodcarving tradition of the New Ireland region, characterized by complex figural compositions and intricate surface decoration.",
  "description": "Malagan carvings feature anthropomorphic and zoomorphic forms with elaborate geometric patterns and symbolic elements, created to commemorate the dead and mark social status. These carvings serve as ritual objects that mediate between the human and spirit worlds, with designs that encode ancestral knowledge and clan histories.",
